tency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.012112057052003036,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":37.4,"_gate_pool_share":0.09896653103779984,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":79.6,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.12116853340175271,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":85.6,"_gate_margins":0.01580070400279539,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":65.8,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.19471933653595339,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.019960381230462065,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":75.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00158,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Corteva, Inc. operates as a pure-play agriculture company in the United States, Canada, the Middle East, Africa, Europe, Latin America, and Asia. The company provides products that protect against weeds, insects, diseases, nematodes, and other pests, as well as supports crop health via nitrogen management and seed-applied technologies. Its crop protection solutions and digital solutions provide farmers tools to improve productivity and help keep fields free of weeds, insects, and diseases. The company offers herbicides, soybeans, cereals, fruits and vegetables, insecticides, nitrogen stabilizers, pasture, and a range management herbicides and biologicals and other nature-based products. The company was incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in Indianapolis, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Luther Clarence Kissam IV | CEO & Director | Age 60","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Corteva, Inc. is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $7.9B market cap on $17.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are expanding by +2.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $2.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 19.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 95% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9519961977186311},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Gear Up for Corteva, Inc. (CTVA) Q3 Earnings: Wall Street Estimates for Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025380/gear-up-for-corteva-inc-ctva-q3-earnings-wall-street-estimates-for-key-metrics?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_preview-3025380","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793970913.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"FMR LLC Discloses 10.3% Ownership Stake in Corteva Inc. as of October 30, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/fmr-llc-discloses-103-ownership-stake-in-corteva-inc-as-of-october-30-2026","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793976853.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"FMR LLC and Abigail P. Johnson Reveal 8.4% Ownership Stake in Corteva as of September 30, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/fmr-llc-and-abigail-p-johnson-reveal-84-ownership-stake-in-corteva-as-of-september-30-2026","date":"2026-11-05","time